@GIGABYTE announced on October 2, 2026, a new 64GB unified-memory version of AI TOP ATOM, expanding the existing 128GB lineup on the NVIDIA DGX Spark platform, the company said in a PR Newswire release from Taipei.

The 64GB configuration keeps the same hardware design and is aimed at developers, researchers, and enterprise teams that want on-premises model inference, prototyping, and data analysis without relying solely on the cloud. Built-in ConnectX-7 networking lets developers cluster up to four units with NVIDIA Sync for a larger memory pool. Software includes the NVIDIA CUDA AI stack plus GIGABYTE AI TOP Utility for model download, inference, and RAG. The 64GB version is officially available starting October 23, 2026; availability, channels, and pricing may vary by region.

Why it matters: named GIGABYTE desktop AI SKU with a dated ship window — irreversible Peak B FACT unused this week. Sources: GIGABYTE / PR Newswire, 2 Oct 2026.

